  "url": "https://science.nasa.gov/earth/earth-observatory/fires-rage-in-georgia/",
  "snippet": "NASA Earth Observatory reports on historic wildfires in Georgia, USA. Two major fires — Pineland Road and Highway 82 — have burned over 50,000 acres (~200 km²) since April 18, 2026, destroying 120+ homes, the most in Georgia's recorded history. Extreme drought conditions fueled rapid spread. Landsat 8 OLI and VIIRS on NOAA-21 captured before/after imagery showing burn scars and active fire fronts.",
